<tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white>Kedge Keep on Saturday, Sept.15 at 6pm EST</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1639&lastnode_id=2320">Pustule</a> on 2001-09-11 23:02:47</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>Greetings to the Horde,<br>
<br>
Since we will be busy this Sunday, ive decided to organize a small raid into Kedge for Epic pieces this Saturday at 6pm EST. Ive already gotten verbal commitments from some of you, and have made a sign up for it at everquestraids.com.  I'll be on a bit earlier for ports, but Id appreciate it if we could all meet at the Gfay spires.  I know this is a horrible place to meet, but as I figure ill be porting many of you its as good a place as any. We can then move down to Dagnors together and form groups.<br>
<br>
A great guide, as well as drop listings, can be found at:<br>
http://www.xegonyalliance.com/resources.html<br>
Our main objective will be to try to take out Phinny for the Mage/Rogue/and Wizard Epics, and the Corrupted/Tainted Seahorse for the Druid Epic.  On our way we'll try to take out as much nameds as we can for loot.<br>
<br>
Because this is my first time into Kedge, im urging that everyone signing up read the FAQ on Kedge. Im keeping it at 18 people max (3 full groups) for the following reasons: 1. Phinny isnt that powerful (51 caster), 2. From what ive read theres alot of tight corridors, the less people to congest them the better, 3. The more people that come, the more disorganized it gets no matter how well you try to control it, 4. Its an entirely underwater zone and many of the mobs are casters who like to dispell (byebye dmf and enduring breath), having less people to worry about 'whos got a waterstone' the better.<br>
<br>
As of now, im sure of at least 1 mage thats coming. This means that if you dont have a fishbone earring or other EB device at least you can rely on waterstones.  Also, try to get your swimming up to par if its lacking (~150 should be great).<br>
<br>
Loot Rules: Subject to change, right now im leaning towards NBG, with the understanding that once youve rolled on/looted something, your out for future rolls UNLESS everyone has already looted or its class specific/nodrop.  If there is a piece that noone wants (since this is all old world stuff) they will go to either SU or BH guildbanks.  Epic pieces (Robe of the Kedge, Staff of Mastery) will be rolled on by the 2-3 highest level people of that class. <br>
<br>
*insert fine print*<br>
As the organizer and probable Raid Leader, im going to be reserving the Wizard Epic piece should it drop for myself (Blue Crystal Staff).  By doing so I will forfeit on any other loot that might drop during this event.</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr>

